    {
      "id": "2ea9c3b6-0b05-47ae-afa4-be195c5575da",
      "question": "What is the most toxicologically relevant form of arsenic for acute poisoning?",
      "answer": "Inorganic trivalent arsenic — As(III) / arsenite. Binds SH groups, inhibits pyruvate dehydrogenase and other key metabolic enzymes.",
