    {
      "id": "7a2567f9-4c30-45ef-8540-8dfb8eb64273",
      "question": "What is the critical difference between Cr(VI) and Cr(III) in toxicology?",
      "answer": "Cr(VI) = hexavalent chromium — potent pulmonary carcinogen, readily enters cells via sulfate/phosphate transporters. Cr(III) = trivalent — essential nutrient, poor cellular uptake, low toxicity.",
