      "video_id": "dose-response-ladder",
      "last_user_answer": "Hazard, dose response, exposure, risk characterization",
      "last_rated_at": "2026-06-01T23:02:40.982465+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "e1fc76fa-f3a5-48ee-a0a2-b7860049d54c",
      "question": "What does Hazard Identification determine?",
      "answer": "Whether an agent CAN cause adverse effects and under what circumstances (qualitative, WoE-based)",
      "collection": "DABT - Risk Assessment",
      "status": "learning",
      "ease_streak": 1,
      "next_review_at": "2026-06-10T12:00:00+00:00",
      "created_at": "2026-05-26T23:48:48.157124+00:00",
      "video_id": "dose-response-ladder",
      "last_user_answer": "Whether a chemical has potential for harm",
      "last_rated_at": "2026-06-01T23:02:40.982465+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "91107ec9-b7c1-43df-baf9-19fd43078867",
      "question": "What does Dose-Response Assessment characterize?",
      "answer": "The quantitative relationship between dose and the incidence/severity of adverse effects",
      "collection": "DABT - Risk Assessment",
      "status": "learning",
      "ease_streak": 1,
      "next_review_at": "2026-06-09T12:00:00+00:00",
      "created_at": "2026-05-26T23:48:48.157124+00:00",
      "video_id": "dose-response-ladder",
      "last_user_answer": "Relationship between increasing dose and toxic response",
      "last_rated_at": "2026-06-01T23:02:40.982465+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "3dbe4cc5-6d49-47b2-b7b6-2b01e0abf345",
      "question": "What does Exposure Assessment estimate?",
      "answer": "The magnitude, frequency, duration, and routes of human or environmental exposure to a toxicant",
      "collection": "DABT - Risk Assessment",
      "status": "learning",
      "ease_streak": 1,
      "next_review_at": "2026-06-10T12:00:00+00:00",
      "created_at": "2026-05-26T23:48:48.157124+00:00",
      "video_id": "dose-response-ladder",
      "last_user_answer": "Amount of exposure a population receives for a toxicant",
      "last_rated_at": "2026-06-01T23:02:40.982465+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "5efce4fe-09c6-4a3a-a8af-1014a73840e2",
      "question": "What does Risk Characterization do?",
      "answer": "Integrates hazard, dose-response, and exposure data to estimate the probability and magnitude of risk",
      "collection": "DABT - Risk Assessment",
      "status": "learning",
      "ease_streak": 1,
      "next_review_at": "2026-06-08T12:00:00+00:00",
      "created_at": "2026-05-26T23:48:48.157124+00:00",
      "video_id": "dose-response-ladder",
      "last_user_answer": "Determines potential risk for specific dose/exposure amounts",
      "last_rated_at": "2026-06-01T23:02:40.982465+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "a683a12d-a442-48bd-837f-a8a2134dd6dc",
      "question": "Define NOAEL.",
      "answer": "No Observed Adverse Effect Level — the highest dose at which no adverse effects are observed in a study",
      "collection": "DABT - Risk Assessment",
      "status": "learning",
      "ease_streak": 0,
      "next_review_at": "2026-06-10T12:00:00+00:00",
      "created_at": "2026-05-26T23:48:48.157124+00:00",
      "video_id": "dose-response-ladder",
      "last_user_answer": "The highest dose at which no adverse effects are observed in a study, the point of departure for calculating the reference dose",
      "last_rated_at": "2026-06-01T23:03:10.230352+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "ddd9f4c8-8a89-4db0-9769-20be7117cb25",
      "question": "Define LOAEL.",
      "answer": "Lowest Observed Adverse Effect Level — the lowest dose at which an adverse effect is observed",
      "collection": "DABT - Risk Assessment",
      "status": "learning",
      "ease_streak": 0,
      "next_review_at": "2026-06-08T21:37:35.987973+00:00",
      "created_at": "2026-05-26T23:48:48.157124+00:00",
      "video_id": "dose-response-ladder",
      "last_user_answer": "Lowest observed adverse effect level",
      "last_rated_at": "2026-06-01T23:03:10.230352+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "a2dba1e7-1eaf-49bb-92fe-2f248ab71a11",
      "question": "What are 4 weaknesses of the NOAEL as a point of departure?",
      "answer": "1. Dose-spacing dependent (must be a tested dose) 2. No confidence interval 3. Ignores slope of dose-response 4. Sample-size dependent",
      "collection": "DABT - Risk Assessment",
      "status": "learning",
      "ease_streak": 0,
      "next_review_at": "2026-06-09T12:00:00+00:00",
      "created_at": "2026-05-26T23:48:48.157124+00:00",
      "video_id": "dose-response-ladder",
      "last_user_answer": "Limited to a dose, doesn't account for slope of toxicity, can be skewed by quality of data, doesn't account for a confidence interval"
    },
    {
      "id": "abdc7077-1410-467b-8ed5-1826ed956764",
      "question": "What distinguishes a NOAEL from a NOEL?",
      "answer": "NOAEL allows non-adverse effects (e.g., mild body weight decrease without histopathology). NOEL requires no effect at all.",
      "collection": "DABT - Risk Assessment",
      "status": "learning",
      "ease_streak": 1,
      "next_review_at": "2026-06-10T12:00:00+00:00",
      "created_at": "2026-05-26T23:48:48.157124+00:00",
      "video_id": "dose-response-ladder",
      "last_user_answer": "Non-observable adverse effect level",
      "last_rated_at": "2026-06-01T23:02:40.982465+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "ccf143e3-47e5-4e82-9ebd-8f6eeb620b1a",
      "question": "Define Benchmark Dose (BMD).",
      "answer": "The dose that produces a pre-specified benchmark response (BMR, e.g., 10% extra risk) as estimated from a fitted statistical dose-response model",
      "collection": "DABT - Risk Assessment",
      "status": "learning",
      "ease_streak": 1,
      "next_review_at": "2026-06-10T12:00:00+00:00",
      "created_at": "2026-05-26T23:48:48.157124+00:00",
      "video_id": "dose-response-ladder",
      "last_user_answer": "Relationship between increasing dose and toxic response",
      "last_rated_at": "2026-06-01T23:03:10.230352+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "804f2a71-c07a-4b50-a9be-12576fa8c564",
      "question": "Define Benchmark Response (BMR).",
      "answer": "The pre-specified effect level used in BMD analysis. Default: 10% extra risk for quantal data, 1 SD for continuous data",
      "collection": "DABT - Risk Assessment",
      "status": "learning",
      "ease_streak": 0,
      "next_review_at": "2026-06-07T23:28:55.878559+00:00",
      "created_at": "2026-05-26T23:48:48.157124+00:00",
      "video_id": "dose-response-ladder",
      "last_user_answer": "10% extra risk above background — correct quantal default, missed 1 SD continuous default",
      "last_rated_at": "2026-06-01T23:03:10.230352+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "f3a1536a-48ef-490c-b088-d2dd7394ef18",
      "question": "Define BMDL.",
      "answer": "Benchmark Dose Lower bound — the 95% lower confidence limit on the BMD. We are 95% confident the true BMD ≥ BMDL",
      "collection": "DABT - Risk Assessment",
      "status": "learning",
      "ease_streak": 1,
      "next_review_at": "2026-06-10T12:00:00+00:00",
      "created_at": "2026-05-26T23:48:48.157124+00:00",
      "video_id": "dose-response-ladder",
      "last_user_answer": "Determines potential risk for specific dose/exposure amounts",
      "last_rated_at": "2026-06-01T23:03:10.230352+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "912f0574-2bbe-4479-b2fb-85f2a0dddc37",
      "question": "Why does EPA use the BMDL rather than the BMD as the POD?",
      "answer": "The BMDL incorporates statistical uncertainty (study quality, sample size, variability). Wider CI = lower BMDL = more conservative",
      "collection": "DABT - Risk Assessment",
      "status": "learning",
      "ease_streak": 0,
      "next_review_at": "2026-06-07T23:29:45.905020+00:00",
      "created_at": "2026-05-26T23:48:48.157124+00:00",
      "video_id": "dose-response-ladder",
      "last_user_answer": "More conservative, accounts for statistical modeling flaws — correct direction, missing 95% lower confidence bound terminology",
      "last_rated_at": "2026-06-01T23:03:10.230352+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "46d892eb-1be7-4713-a6a4-ad52782c9660",
      "question": "What does a wide gap between BMD and BMDL indicate?",
      "answer": "High uncertainty in the dose-response data (small sample size, high variability, poor model fit)",
      "collection": "DABT - Risk Assessment",
      "status": "learning",
      "ease_streak": 1,
      "next_review_at": "2026-06-08T23:02:40.982465+00:00",
      "created_at": "2026-05-26T23:48:48.157124+00:00",
      "video_id": "dose-response-ladder",
      "last_user_answer": "Benchmark Dose and Benchmark Dose Lower, preferred due to statistical modeling",
      "last_rated_at": "2026-06-01T23:02:40.982465+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "faa56b84-1aa1-41e8-b568-1f181ae38e1a",
      "question": "When does EPA accept NOAEL as POD instead of BMDL?",
      "answer": "When dose-response data are insufficient for BMD modeling (e.g., only 2 dose groups, poor model fit)",
      "collection": "DABT - Risk Assessment",
      "status": "learning",
      "ease_streak": 1,
      "next_review_at": "2026-06-09T12:00:00+00:00",
      "created_at": "2026-05-26T23:48:48.157124+00:00",
      "video_id": "dose-response-ladder",
      "last_user_answer": "Non-observable adverse effect level",
      "last_rated_at": "2026-06-01T23:03:10.230352+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "79dd1252-b7dd-4dbe-b58c-af4975aeb15c",
      "question": "Define Point of Departure (POD).",
      "answer": "The point on the dose-response curve used as the starting point for low-dose extrapolation. Can be NOAEL, LOAEL, BMDL, or BMD",
      "collection": "DABT - Risk Assessment",
      "status": "learning",
      "ease_streak": 1,
      "next_review_at": "2026-06-08T23:03:10.230352+00:00",
      "created_at": "2026-05-26T23:48:48.157124+00:00",
      "video_id": "dose-response-ladder",
      "last_user_answer": "Lowest observable adverse effect level",
      "last_rated_at": "2026-06-01T23:03:10.230352+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "f2030717-9cdc-4878-a369-96a05d504a18",
      "question": "Define Uncertainty Factors (UFs) in risk assessment.",
      "answer": "Factors applied to the POD to account for gaps in data and uncertainty in extrapolation from study conditions to real-world human populations",
      "collection": "DABT - Risk Assessment",
      "status": "learning",
      "ease_streak": 0,
      "next_review_at": "2026-06-08T21:38:33.897381+00:00",
      "created_at": "2026-05-26T23:48:48.157124+00:00",
      "video_id": "dose-response-ladder",
      "last_user_answer": "Divisors applied to POD for uncertainty in extrapolation from study conditions to real-world human populations",
      "last_rated_at": "2026-06-01T23:03:10.230352+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "a5d87110-872d-4870-aa18-05be0e55d3f1",
      "question": "What is the default total UF for a chronic animal NOAEL to human RfD?",
      "answer": "100× = UFₐ (10× interspecies) × UFₕ (10× intraspecies)",
      "collection": "DABT - Risk Assessment",
      "status": "learning",
      "ease_streak": 1,
      "next_review_at": "2026-06-10T12:00:00+00:00",
      "created_at": "2026-05-26T23:48:48.157124+00:00",
      "video_id": "dose-response-ladder",
      "last_user_answer": "Non-observable adverse effect level",
      "last_rated_at": "2026-06-01T23:02:40.982465+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "d2834079-e82b-4e47-8409-6a104b9ef917",
      "question": "What is the default total UF for a subchronic animal NOAEL to human RfD?",
      "answer": "1000× = UFₐ (10) × UFₕ (10) × UFₛ (10)",
      "collection": "DABT - Risk Assessment",
      "status": "learning",
      "ease_streak": 1,
      "next_review_at": "2026-06-10T12:00:00+00:00",
      "created_at": "2026-05-26T23:48:48.157124+00:00",
      "video_id": "dose-response-ladder",
      "last_user_answer": "Non-observable adverse effect level",
      "last_rated_at": "2026-06-01T23:02:40.982465+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "56ab79e7-2274-473a-b280-50633aaec401",
      "question": "What does UFₐ (10×) account for?",
      "answer": "Interspecies extrapolation — differences between test animals and humans in toxicokinetics (4×) and toxicodynamics (2.5×)",
      "collection": "DABT - Risk Assessment",
      "status": "learning",
      "ease_streak": 1,
      "next_review_at": "2026-06-08T12:00:00+00:00",
      "created_at": "2026-05-26T23:48:48.157124+00:00",
      "video_id": "dose-response-ladder",
      "last_user_answer": "Point of departure dose divided by uncertainty factor",
      "last_rated_at": "2026-06-01T23:03:10.230352+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "6f6f969b-cc60-45a2-9e88-6a136c474acb",
      "question": "Decompose the 10× interspecies UF into its two components.",
      "answer": "TK = 10^0.6 ≈ 4× (clearance, metabolism, distribution). TD = 10^0.4 ≈ 2.5× (target tissue sensitivity)",
      "collection": "DABT - Risk Assessment",
      "status": "learning",
      "ease_streak": 1,
      "next_review_at": "2026-06-08T23:03:10.230352+00:00",
      "created_at": "2026-05-26T23:48:48.157124+00:00",
      "video_id": "dose-response-ladder",
      "last_user_answer": "Benchmark Dose and Benchmark Dose Lower, preferred due to statistical modeling",
      "last_rated_at": "2026-06-01T23:03:10.230352+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "fc52d442-4b0f-4412-bdc4-1dfb0b77c126",
      "question": "Decompose the 10× intraspecies UF into its two components.",
      "answer": "TK = 10^0.5 ≈ 3.2× (individual differences in metabolism/clearance). TD = 10^0.5 ≈ 3.2× (individual differences in tissue sensitivity)",
      "collection": "DABT - Risk Assessment",
      "status": "learning",
      "ease_streak": 1,
      "next_review_at": "2026-06-10T00:24:57.971748+00:00",
      "created_at": "2026-05-26T23:48:48.157124+00:00",
      "video_id": "dose-response-ladder",
      "last_user_answer": "Toxicodynamics and toxicokinetics, 3.2 times 3.2 for both",
      "last_rated_at": "2026-06-01T23:03:10.230352+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "100f8e6d-f22d-4fec-8a6b-686aedb21fe4",
      "question": "What does UFₛ account for?",
      "answer": "Subchronic-to-chronic extrapolation — effects that may appear only after longer exposure (accumulation, late-manifesting pathology)",
      "collection": "DABT - Risk Assessment",
      "status": "learning",
      "ease_streak": 1,
      "next_review_at": "2026-06-08T12:00:00+00:00",
      "created_at": "2026-05-26T23:48:48.157124+00:00",
      "video_id": "dose-response-ladder",
      "last_user_answer": "RfD is oral, RfC is for inhalation",
      "last_rated_at": "2026-06-01T23:03:10.230352+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "093f7734-d2b4-44d1-9a95-f4e0329b89ac",
      "question": "What does UF_L account for?",
      "answer": "LOAEL-to-NOAEL extrapolation — used when the POD is a LOAEL rather than a NOAEL (default up to 10×)",
      "collection": "DABT - Risk Assessment",
      "status": "learning",
      "ease_streak": 0,
      "next_review_at": "2026-06-09T12:00:00+00:00",
      "created_at": "2026-05-26T23:48:48.157124+00:00",
      "video_id": "dose-response-ladder",
      "last_user_answer": "NOAEL to LOAEL — direction reversed, should be LOAEL to NOAEL",
      "last_rated_at": "2026-06-01T23:03:10.230352+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "e147a5d0-5c1c-4667-9826-8de5ec96080e",
      "question": "Define Modifying Factor (MF).",
      "answer": "An additional factor (1-10×) applied for study quality concerns, database deficiencies, or other uncertainties not captured by standard UFs",
      "collection": "DABT - Risk Assessment",
      "status": "learning",
      "ease_streak": 1,
      "next_review_at": "2026-06-09T12:00:00+00:00",
      "created_at": "2026-05-26T23:48:48.157124+00:00",
      "video_id": "dose-response-ladder",
      "last_user_answer": "Genotoxic = linear, non-genotoxic = dependent on data/non-linear threshold",
      "last_rated_at": "2026-06-01T23:03:10.230352+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "fdd29411-ddab-43c2-9bff-42104aaff210",
      "question": "Define CSAF (Chemical-Specific Adjustment Factor).",
      "answer": "A data-derived factor that replaces a default UF component (e.g., using PBPK data to replace the default 4× TK component of UFₐ)",
      "collection": "DABT - Risk Assessment",
      "status": "learning",
      "ease_streak": 0,
      "next_review_at": "2026-06-07T23:31:33.719572+00:00",
      "created_at": "2026-05-26T23:48:48.157124+00:00",
      "video_id": "dose-response-ladder",
      "last_user_answer": "Chemical-specific data, affects TK/TD portion of UF — correct, missing replaces-default-UF-component precision",
      "last_rated_at": "2026-06-01T23:03:10.230352+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "1a140ee4-1ecd-4a19-9fd8-a925c17ce91e",
      "question": "Can PBPK data reduce multiple UFs simultaneously?",
      "answer": "Yes — a single PBPK model can inform UFₐ_TK (species differences) AND UFₕ_TK (human variability) if the model includes a population distribution",
      "collection": "DABT - Risk Assessment",
      "status": "learning",
      "ease_streak": 1,
      "next_review_at": "2026-06-08T23:03:10.230352+00:00",
      "created_at": "2026-05-26T23:48:48.157124+00:00",
      "video_id": "dose-response-ladder",
      "last_user_answer": "Given exposure divided by RfD, >1 hazardous, <1 safe",
      "last_rated_at": "2026-06-01T23:03:10.230352+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "e1a24c05-5725-4fb1-b267-478374c12e03",
      "question": "Define Reference Dose (RfD).",
      "answer": "An estimate of daily oral exposure to the human population (including sensitive subgroups) likely without appreciable risk of adverse effects over a lifetime",
      "collection": "DABT - Risk Assessment",
      "status": "learning",
      "ease_streak": 1,
      "next_review_at": "2026-06-08T23:03:10.230352+00:00",
      "created_at": "2026-05-26T23:48:48.157124+00:00",
      "video_id": "dose-response-ladder",
      "last_user_answer": "Sum of hazard quotients of multiple chemicals",
      "last_rated_at": "2026-06-01T23:03:10.230352+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "753bf33b-0fa7-45a2-b7fc-152d804ffc01",
      "question": "How is an RfD calculated?",
      "answer": "RfD = POD / UF_total. Example: BMDL₁₀ of 7.8 mg/kg ÷ 57 UF = 0.137 mg/kg/day",
      "collection": "DABT - Risk Assessment",
      "status": "learning",
      "ease_streak": 1,
      "next_review_at": "2026-06-08T23:03:10.230352+00:00",
      "created_at": "2026-05-26T23:48:48.157124+00:00",
      "video_id": "dose-response-ladder",
      "last_user_answer": "Absorption, distribution, metabolism, excretion",
      "last_rated_at": "2026-06-01T23:03:10.230352+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "bb52e0e5-78c4-4bc6-ad24-e824572d31c3",
      "question": "Define Reference Concentration (RfC).",
      "answer": "Same concept as RfD but for inhalation exposure. Units: mg/m³ instead of mg/kg/day",
      "collection": "DABT - Risk Assessment",
      "status": "learning",
      "ease_streak": 1,
      "next_review_at": "2026-06-08T23:03:10.230352+00:00",
      "created_at": "2026-05-26T23:48:48.157124+00:00",
      "video_id": "dose-response-ladder",
      "last_user_answer": "Limited to the doses tested",
      "last_rated_at": "2026-06-01T23:03:10.230352+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "11441890-0b12-46fa-adc7-3ed284ba6980",
      "question": "Define Acceptable Daily Intake (ADI).",
      "answer": "Essentially the same as RfD — the safe daily dose. Used specifically for food additives and pesticide residues (WHO/FAO/FDA)",
      "collection": "DABT - Risk Assessment",
      "status": "learning",
      "ease_streak": 1,
      "next_review_at": "2026-06-08T23:03:10.230352+00:00",
      "created_at": "2026-05-26T23:48:48.157124+00:00",
      "video_id": "dose-response-ladder",
      "last_user_answer": "10x, accounts for toxicokinetics and toxicodynamics",
      "last_rated_at": "2026-06-01T23:03:10.230352+00:00"
    },
    {
      "id": "a37482a9-adae-42a7-b0e9-291347c6c806",
      "question": "What is the difference between RfD and ADI?",
      "answer": "Same concept (safe daily dose). RfD is EPA terminology for environmental contaminants. ADI is WHO/FAO terminology for food additives/pesticides",
      "collection": "DABT - Risk Assessment",
      "status": "learning",
      "ease_streak": 0,
