    },
    {
      "id": "5591f6db-d8c2-46ee-9d1b-93ca166dcf19",
      "question": "Give an example of Phase I bioactivation and Phase II detoxification.",
      "answer": "Phase I bioactivation: CCl4 metabolized by CYP2E1 to trichloromethyl radical (.CCl3) causing lipid peroxidation and hepatotoxicity. Phase II detoxification: Glutathione conjugation of NAPQI (APAP metabolite) protects the liver from oxidative damage.",
