      "video_id": "domain-i-blocks1-2-supplement",
      "last_user_answer": null
    },
    {
      "id": "3442ccee-812d-4ad2-8a54-50a7e743951e",
      "question": "What is the half-life formula and the directional relationships between its variables?",
      "answer": "t1/2 = 0.693 x Vd / CL. CL decreases — t1/2 increases (inverse). Vd increases — t1/2 increases (direct). A compound with high Vd AND low CL has the longest half-lives (years for TCDD, PCBs).",
      "collection": "DABT - Conduct of Studies",
      "status": "learning",
      "ease_streak": 0,
      "next_review_at": "2026-06-08T20:04:38.076043+00:00",
      "created_at": "2026-05-29T20:04:30.849042+00:00",
      "video_id": "domain-i-blocks1-2-supplement",
      "last_user_answer": null
    },
    {
      "id": "21d52677-11bb-4178-8e7a-ceb598868d56",
      "question": "What is the formula for oral bioavailability (F) and how does hepatic extraction ratio (E) affect it?",
      "answer": "F = (AUC_oral / AUC_iv) x 100%, or for completely absorbed drugs: F = 1 - E. High E (>0.7) — low F (<0.3) — absorption limited by first-pass metabolism. Low E (<0.3) — high F (>0.7) — most drug survives first pass.",
      "collection": "DABT - Conduct of Studies",
      "status": "learning",
      "ease_streak": 0,
      "next_review_at": "2026-06-09T20:04:38.076043+00:00",
      "created_at": "2026-05-29T20:04:30.849042+00:00",
      "video_id": "domain-i-blocks1-2-supplement",
      "last_user_answer": null
    },
    {
      "id": "f84621df-e581-462b-a4f6-f5e62ca75a46",
      "question": "SD vs SE: which describes variability among individual animals in a group, and which describes precision of the mean estimate?",
      "answer": "SD (standard deviation) = individual animal variability. SE (standard error of the mean) = precision of the mean estimate. SE = SD/√n, so SE shrinks with larger n even if biological variability is unchanged. ABT exam trap: reporting SE as if it describes sample dispersion.",
      "collection": "DABT - Conduct of Studies",
      "status": "learning",
      "ease_streak": 0,
      "next_review_at": "2026-06-09T12:00:00+00:00",
