      "video_id": "conduct-of-studies-block3-stats",
      "last_user_answer": null
    },
    {
      "id": "53a4a2fb-f3b6-4334-b9f3-938f4b17f270",
      "question": "A 3-group repeated-dose study (control, low, high) measures serum ALT (continuous, normal). Which statistical test is appropriate for comparing means across all groups, and which post-hoc test is standard for comparing each dose to control?",
      "answer": "ANOVA (tests if at least one group differs). Dunnett's test for post-hoc comparisons of each dose group vs. control. Dunnett's is the toxicology standard because it accounts for correlation among comparisons sharing the same control — less conservative than Bonferroni.",
      "collection": "DABT - Conduct of Studies",
      "status": "learning",
      "ease_streak": 0,
      "next_review_at": "2026-06-09T12:00:00+00:00",
